ath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T09:13:55-07:00","id":669754,"title":"","content":"@Xenowrath Well at least we have online converters, otherwise I would never figure this stuff out.<br /> <br /> @FallenEco I'll make the group real quick and then I can pm you all the url.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","name":"kajedhorrors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:44:21-07:00","id":670396,"title":"","content":"Got the link, thanks. Anyone else brainstorming character ideas already?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T18:50:44-07:00","id":670397,"title":"","content":"I've got a couple, depending on the setting and group dynamics...<br /> <br /> In other news my 'testing' of Roll20 has revealed that it has a problem with my cookies settings. Attempting to fix before 'crunch time'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-18-2015, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T20:15:50-07:00","id":670436,"title":"","content":"Some base concepts rattling around in my head:<br /> <br /> *an Ugallu urban explorer/graffiti artist, who steals by necessity, and feeds his Hunger for Ruin by painting materpieces on buildings, then burning them down a day later.<br /> *a Nemesis whose particular &quot;flavor&quot; is punishing cruelty to animals, usually in viciously ironic ways. Not sure what family, or have much of a personality yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:05:39-07:00","id":670450,"title":"","content":"I've got some ideas, but nothing concrete. The one I really liked is slipping my mind at the moment, but hopefully I'll remember it tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:11:03-07:00","id":670452,"title":"","content":"How would that work for a Nemesis? I don't think from animals and not everyone cares for an animals enough to associate the creature's suffering with their own actions? Unless I read Nemesis wrong, the subject of the Feeding needs to be aware they have 'done wrong'. Like how the subject of a Tyrant's Feeding needs to submit or how a Predator needs to take a trophy to show the 'hunt' was a success.<br /> <br /> Actually, I've just looked it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Latest Draft; Chapter 1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Whatever the exact method used, the victim must be made aware of exactly what rule he broke, and know that his infraction is why such awful things are happening to him. Punishment simply isn\u2019t satisfying to a Nemesis if the victim isn\u2019t aware that they have earned their pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not criticizing, just really curious as to how that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T21:19:49-07:00","id":670455,"title":"","content":"Well, of course they didn't think they were doing wrong at the time they did it, or they wouldn't have done it. It's on me to make it clear to them that yes, you are being punished for running a dog-fighting ring, or killing a little kid's cat to get at their parent, or rounding up rattlesnakes to kill them because &quot;they're icky&quot; or whatever. Note it doesn't say the victim has to agree that they deserve the punishment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T10:02:44-07:00","id":671041,"title":"","content":"Yeah the crime doesn't have to actually even be something anyone else would consider evil. You could just punish people for stepping on cracks in the sidewalk or stepping off the path in the forest.<br /> You just have to, one way or another, tell your victim what they're being punished for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","name":"kajedhorrors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:54:12-07:00","id":672215,"title":"","content":"Are we keeping the same time slot for next week?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T22:08:10-07:00","id":673859,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> I've enjoyed all of your company so far, and hope you can all make it to successive sessions. As far as I know, the same time slot will work in the future.<br /> <br /> @GottaGoFeast: if you get time during the week, I'd like it if you could fill out that questionnaire on the second page of the character sheet.<br /> <br /> @FallenEcho: you're missing the last question on the aforementioned questionnaire, if you could take a look at that I would appreciate it.<br /> <br /> @All of my players: Upon some thinking I've decided to set the game in <b>Baltimore, Maryland.</b> As long as nobody has any objections (I don't know why they would, I just felt the need to say), the game will be set in Baltimore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","name":"kajedhorrors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T18:01:02-07:00","id":674756,"title":"","content":"Cool. As someone who lives in an adjacent state but has never been to Baltimore, anything we should know about the city beforehand? Particularly your version of the supernatural side?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T23:09:14-07:00","id":674954,"title":"","content":"I'll probably either do some exposition or put together a one-sheet type thing<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],